[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2594210451","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101617#issuecomment-2594210451","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101617","id":2594210451,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aoIKT","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T00:32:40Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T00:32:40Z","body":"There are some more issues with #100113 and its follow-up #101537:\r\n- #101537 removed the signal disconnect, but not the previous two lines which you just added to be able to disconnect the signal. These should be removed too. But I wonder: when is the signal disconnected now? What happens if you set the same ParticleProcessMaterial twice in a GPUParticles3D? Won't it error that the signal is already connected? The way we handle this usually is that the `set_process_material` setter should first check if the current material needs the signal disconnected, before assigning the new material and connecting the signal.\r\n- The signal is emitted only in `TOOLS_ENABLED`, but this isn't documented, and there's still code like here that connects it in non-TOOLS_ENABLED builds.\r\n- Finally there's #101611 which is why I started looking into #100113, but the above nitpicks don't seem to be what's causing the crash. I haven't had time to investigate further yet.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2594210451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596824162","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101617#issuecomment-2596824162","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101617","id":2596824162,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ayGRi","user":{"login":"paddy-exe","id":38077837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MDc3ODM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38077837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe","html_url":"https://github.com/paddy-exe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paddy-exe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T20:24:43Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T20:27:17Z","body":"Alright, I think I have solved the problem with `ShaderMaterial` and the signal connect and disconnect. Also added a documentation note in the class reference. In the `CurveEdit` class at least when setting a new curve you disconnect the signals and then re-add them to the new assigned one (see [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d33da79d3f8fe84be2521d25b9ba8e440cf25a88/editor/plugins/curve_editor_plugin.cpp#L59)) so I took inspiration from that.\r\n\r\nI tested the various problem cases removing and re-adding the same material, adding a ShaderMaterial instead, using the same material on several GPUParticles3D Nodes and haven't encountered any errors or crashes (together with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101636 that is).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596824162/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2598729579","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101617#issuecomment-2598729579","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101617","id":2598729579,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a5Xdr","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users